{% comment %}
  Starts from Shopify's own robots rules so the platform's crawl-budget
  protections (checkout, cart, account, search noise) stay intact, then:

  1. Re-allows /policies/, which Shopify disallows by default. The store's
     shipping, refund, privacy and terms pages live there and are the
     canonical copies, so they must be readable - both for shoppers'
     assistants and for review of the store's stated policies.
  2. Explicitly allows the AI crawlers. Without an explicit allow several
     of these treat "unlisted" as "unavailable".

  Whitespace matters in this file: each directive has to land on its own
  line, so the tags below deliberately do not strip newlines.
{% endcomment %}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
{{ group.user_agent }}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{% unless rule.directive == 'Disallow' and rule.value contains '/policies/' %}{{ rule }}
{% endunless %}{% endfor %}Allow: /policies/
{% if group.sitemap %}{{ group.sitemap }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
# AI assistants and answer engines: allowed to read the catalogue and the
# policies so they can recommend and quote this store accurately.
